<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Brooke returns three months after his last visit, about nine and a half months into tamoxifen and ten months after surgery. He has missed no doses. Hot flashes remain mild; libido is unchanged and he is not troubled by it. He has had no leg swelling or pain, chest pain, breathlessness, or change in vision, and no new lump, skin change, or swelling on either side of the chest or in either armpit, no bone pain, cough, or weight loss. Since his last visit he has begun speaking publicly about breast cancer in men, to encourage men to have a lump or discomfort in the chest checked and to ask their doctors to examine them. He walks most days and feels well. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tamoxifen</td><td>About nine and a half months; no missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Side effects</td><td>Mild hot flashes; lower libido, not bothersome</td></tr><tr><td>Recurrence symptoms</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Independent; walking most days; busy with speaking and writing</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

