    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Right breast cancer, stage IIA, no evidence of recurrence (C50.121)</content>. No symptoms or signs of recurrence ten months after surgery. Surveillance continues on the CMID and ACS/ASCO schedule. [S]<list><item>Written survivorship care plan given today: treatment summary, the tamoxifen plan, the surveillance schedule, symptoms to report, and whom to call.</item><item>History and examination every three to six months to three years, then every six to twelve months to five years, then yearly.</item><item>No routine imaging, blood tests, or tumor markers unless symptoms arise.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Long-term tamoxifen (Z79.810)</content>. Well tolerated with good adherence. [S]<list><item>Continue tamoxifen 20 mg daily; at five years, Dr. Cho will discuss whether to extend it.</item><item>DXA again in eighteen months.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Cancer-related history and examination of both sides of the chest wall and both axillae</td><td>Every 3 to 6 months for 3 years</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No evidence of recurrence</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Lymphedema assessment</td><td>Every visit after axillary surgery</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No arm swelling</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Venous thromboembolism symptoms on tamoxifen</td><td>Every visit on tamoxifen</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Hot flashes on tamoxifen</td><td>Every visit on tamoxifen</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mild</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Sexual side effects of tamoxifen</td><td>Every visit on tamoxifen</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Lower libido, stable; no treatment wanted</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence to tamoxifen</td><td>Every visit on tamoxifen</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Distress and depression screen (PHQ-2)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Fatigue and cognitive concerns</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Bone density (DXA)</td><td>Every 2 years on hormone therapy</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Six months ago; next in eighteen months</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Breast imaging (mammography)</td><td>Yearly only for a remaining breast after lumpectomy, or the other breast with a predisposing variant</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Both breasts were removed; there is no breast tissue to image</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Routine blood tests, tumor markers, and CT, bone scan, or PET</td><td>Not recommended without symptoms in stage I to III disease</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No symptoms suggesting recurrence</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Survivorship care plan and lifestyle counseling</td><td>Within a year of treatment; lifestyle every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Written plan given; at least 150 minutes of activity a week; no tobacco or alcohol</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Take tamoxifen every day with side effects managed, aiming to continue for at least five years. Outcome by 2026-08-11: No missed doses by pill count over seven months; mild hot flashes and a mild fall in libido, both manageable; no clot symptoms [S]</item><item>Complete germline genetic testing with counseling, and give him written information for his relatives. Outcome by 2026-05-12: No pathogenic variant in a multigene panel; family letter given [S]</item><item>Establish bone health on hormone therapy at his age: DXA, vitamin D of 30 ng/mL or more, and weight-bearing exercise. Outcome by 2026-05-12: Femoral neck T-score -1.2; vitamin D 36 ng/mL after supplementation [S]</item><item>Give a written survivorship care plan with the surveillance schedule. Outcome by 2026-08-11: Survivorship care plan given at the survivorship visit [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Hassett MJ, et al. Management of Male Breast Cancer: ASCO Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2020;38(16):1849-1863 (2020); Runowicz CD, et al. American Cancer Society/American Society of Clinical Oncology Breast Cancer Survivorship Care Guideline. CA Cancer J Clin 2016;66(1):43-73 (2016); Shapiro CL, et al. Management of Osteoporosis in Survivors of Adult Cancers With Nonmetastatic Disease: ASCO Clinical Practice Guideline (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Annual wellness visit in two months. Survivorship visit in three to six months. Medical oncology every six months. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-13: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
